---
import MainLayout from '../../layouts/MainLayout.astro';
---

<MainLayout title="Password Reset | Salesdam Docs" description="Password reset and security guide">
  <div class="content-wrapper">
    <h1>Password Reset & Security</h1>

    <p class="intro">Learn how to reset your password, manage security settings, and protect your account.</p>

    <h2>Resetting Your Password</h2>

    <h3>Method 1: Using Login Page</h3>
    <ol>
      <li>Go to the Salesdam login page</li>
      <li>Click "Forgot Password?" link</li>
      <li>Enter your email address</li>
      <li>Click "Send Reset Link"</li>
      <li>Check your email for the reset link</li>
      <li>Click the link (valid for 24 hours)</li>
      <li>Enter your new password</li>
      <li>Click "Reset Password"</li>
    </ol>

    <h3>Method 2: From Account Settings</h3>
    <ol>
      <li>Log in to your Salesdam account</li>
      <li>Go to Settings → Account Security</li>
      <li>Click "Change Password"</li>
      <li>Enter your current password</li>
      <li>Enter and confirm your new password</li>
      <li>Click "Update Password"</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Password Requirements</h2>

    <table>
      <tr>
        <th>Requirement</th>
        <th>Details</th>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Minimum Length</td>
        <td>8 characters</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Uppercase Letters</td>
        <td>At least one A-Z</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Lowercase Letters</td>
        <td>At least one a-z</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Numbers</td>
        <td>Recommended but not required</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Special Characters</td>
        <td>Recommended but not required</td>
      </tr>
    </table>

    <h2>Password Best Practices</h2>

    <ul>
      <li>✓ Use a unique password not used elsewhere</li>
      <li>✓ Use a mix of uppercase, lowercase, and numbers</li>
      <li>✓ Use a passphrase rather than a single word</li>
      <li>✓ Change your password every 90 days</li>
      <li>✗ Never share your password</li>
      <li>✗ Don't use personal information (birthdate, name)</li>
      <li>✗ Don't reuse old passwords</li>
      <li>✗ Don't write passwords down in plain text</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Account Security Settings</h2>

    <h3>Two-Factor Authentication (2FA)</h3>
    <p>Enable 2FA to add an extra layer of security to your account:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Go to Settings → Account Security</li>
      <li>Click "Enable Two-Factor Authentication"</li>
      <li>Choose authentication method:
        <ul>
          <li>Authenticator App (Google Authenticator, Microsoft Authenticator)</li>
          <li>SMS (Text message to your phone)</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li>Follow the setup instructions</li>
      <li>Save your backup codes in a safe place</li>
    </ol>

    <div class="warning">
      <strong>⚠️ Important:</strong> Save your backup codes. You'll need them if you lose access to your 2FA device.
    </div>

    <h2>Session Management</h2>

    <h3>Active Sessions</h3>
    <p>View and manage all your active sessions:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Go to Settings → Account Security</li>
      <li>Scroll to "Active Sessions"</li>
      <li>See all devices logged into your account</li>
      <li>Click "Sign Out" to end a session</li>
      <li>Click "Sign Out All" to logout everywhere</li>
    </ol>

    <h3>Session Information</h3>
    <table>
      <tr>
        <th>Column</th>
        <th>Description</th>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Device</td>
        <td>Browser and operating system</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Location</td>
        <td>Approximate geographic location</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>IP Address</td>
        <td>Your internet connection's IP</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Last Active</td>
        <td>When this session was last used</td>
      </tr>
    </table>

    <h2>Suspicious Activity</h2>

    <p>If you notice suspicious activity on your account:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Immediately change your password</li>
      <li>Review your active sessions</li>
      <li>Sign out any unrecognized sessions</li>
      <li>Contact support with details</li>
      <li>Check for unauthorized API token access</li>
    </ol>

    <div class="note">
      <strong>📞 Support:</strong> Email support@salesdam.com for security concerns.
    </div>

    <h2>API Tokens</h2>

    <h3>Creating an API Token</h3>
    <ol>
      <li>Go to Settings → API Tokens</li>
      <li>Click "Create New Token"</li>
      <li>Give it a descriptive name</li>
      <li>Choose permissions it should have</li>
      <li>Set an expiration date (optional)</li>
      <li>Click "Create Token"</li>
      <li>Copy and store the token securely</li>
    </ol>

    <h3>Managing API Tokens</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Regenerate tokens regularly</li>
      <li>Revoke unused tokens</li>
      <li>Set expiration dates</li>
      <li>Use different tokens for different purposes</li>
      <li>Never commit tokens to version control</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="success">
      <strong>✓ Secured!</strong> Your account is now protected. For more information, see <a href="/api/authentication">API Authentication</a>.
    </div>
  </div>
</MainLayout>
